n liquid fuel policy and facilitation of industry investment; (f) the provision and distribution of infrastructure required to support the Government's ambitious targets for the uptake of electric vehicles to diversify the Australian light car fleet; and (g) any related matters. Sue Lines The question is that business of the Senate No. 1, standing in the name of Senator McKenzie and others, be agreed to.","result":"negative","slug":"division-federal-senate-10069","source_url":"https://theyvoteforyou.org.au/divisions/senate/2026-03-12/11"}
